        "original_id": "4f873034-845f-5680-acdb-b85b3f8bbdb0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: The Postal Service, Missio\n- People: Ben Gibbard, Jimmy Tamborello, Jenny Lewis, Matthew Brue, David Butler\n- Song: “We Will Become Silhouettes”\n- Place: Seattle, Washington\n- Record Label: Sub Pop Records\n\nFacts:\n- The Postal Service were an American indie rock band from Seattle, Washington.\n- The Postal Service consisted of vocalist Ben Gibbard, producer Jimmy Tamborello, and Jenny Lewis on background vocals.\n- Ben Gibbard was also associated with Death Cab for Cutie.\n- Jimmy Tamborello was also associated with Dntel and Headset.\n- Jenny Lewis was also associated with Rilo Kiley.\n- “We Will Become Silhouettes” is a single by The Postal Service that was released on February 8, 2005.\n- “We Will Become Silhouettes” was released under the Sub Pop Records label.\n- Missio currently consists of founding member Matthew Brue and David Butler.\n- Matthew Brue performs vocals and production roles in Missio.\n- David Butler performs producer and instrumentalist roles in Missio.",
